# Every expression statement of the norm (CODEX-FABLE-HEADLESS-DOC-20260923-01), each through the
# one consumer: bare `2`, `2 + 2`, `hits + 1` (a field read, dropped), a bare callable `f`
# (called), `(f)` (called), `(2 + 2)`, an empty `()`, and the anonymous vertical forms of the
# last three.  f counts its calls: f, (f) and the vertical (f) -- 3.
int: hits 0

fn: f () int
    hits: hits + 1
    return: 7
end: f

2
2 + 2
hits + 1
f
(f)
(2 + 2)
()
(
. 2 + 2
)
(
. f
)
(
)
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: hits; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
